sentences.l:
And down from a peg he hung the clear-sounding lyre,
and of Demodocus he took the hand and led him out of the hall,
the herald;

In stature indeed he is not bad,
in thighs and calves and both hands above,
in sturdy neck and great strength;

For one man is slighter in form,
but a god crowns his shape with words, and they, at him,
taking delight, look;

and down they cowered to the ground,
the long-oared Phaeacians, ship-famous men,
under the rush of the stone;
